; Direct tests of the helpers the stages share: the traversals of the TST and
; the CGT (traversals.ml), types and their substitution, signatures, overload
; ranking, lowering's type layouts, the runtime's ABI and what its structs
; measure (tests/runtime/abi), what stage 5's evaluator makes of the tree,
; what LLVM is told about each runtime function, how codegen reads a snapshot, which loops it marks to be unrolled, which lists a loop reads once before it and whose pushes' room it makes first, which loops strip mining cuts into runs (loops.ml), the processor codegen tunes for and which targets it accepts, and
; how a build keeps its compiled runtime and links. The golden suites test the
; same code end to end; these show which helper broke, rather than where in a
; golden file the difference surfaced. They also check that semantics run twice in one process gives the
; same tree (it keeps no numbering from one check to the next), that the
; test rules' generator pairs every fixture with a golden file, and that the
; driver checks a stamp and keeps a file its rewrite did not create, and the
; C interface's front half (foreign_c.ml): `c.coda`'s patterns and paths,
; a C compiler's include list, a C source compiled by the linked
; clang, a global an `__asm__` label names read by its label, a Mach-O
; alias renamed with its target, a dependency's C module made a retained
; copy, the file of C module hashes beside an object and its rows, and the glue's
; thunks in the order of their labels. It also checks that the arrays codegen
; reads from LLVM survive a collection when empty, and that no compiler source
; reads them through the bindings' own, which corrupt the heap then, and
; that no compiler source disposes an LLVM context except through
; Contexts.dispose. It checks that every intrinsic has a description for the language server, and
; that a hover hides the parameters the checker supplies.
;
; Overloads, State, Type_layout, Emit, Build and stage 5's modules are not re-exported by their libraries'
; entry modules, so they are reached by the names dune gives them.

(test
 (name unit)
 (modules (:standard \ builder_after_context))
 (libraries cache cgt codegen diagnostic driver foreign fixture_pairing llvm llvm_analysis llvm_bitreader llvm_bitwriter llvm_irreader llvm_target optimize rewrite source sst tree_graph tst unix)
 (deps
  ../../runtime/zane.h
  ../runtime/abi/probe.out
  (source_tree ../codegen/fixtures/lambdas)
  (source_tree ../../lib)))

; A builder dropped while its context lives is finalized before the context
; is disposed (lib/codegen/contexts.ml). The program runs natively here;
; tests/runtime/valgrind_test.py runs it under Valgrind, which reports a
; builder finalized after its context.

(executable
 (name builder_after_context)
 (modules builder_after_context)
 (libraries codegen llvm llvm_irreader))

(rule
 (alias runtest)
 (action
  (run %{exe:builder_after_context.exe})))
